   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In order to select the gene features, that will be used for training, we implement 2 main strategies. \n",
    "\n",
    "1. We select the top 2000 highly variable genes, specified as `n_hvgs` at the start of the notebook. \n",
    "\n",
    "2. The authors of the publication _\"...performed pooled Perturb-CITE-seq screens of ICR program genes in a patient-derived tumor–TIL co-culture model, targeting 248 genes of the ICR signature (744 targeting guides)...\"_. As such, we the `adata.obs` column `guide_id` to filter out all genes, that have been targeted and could carry information regarding the perturbation condition. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "f786eb0c-4a48-40bc-b5f8-9bbe63cdab8a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "gene_features:  2154\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Strategy 1: HVGs\n",
    "hvg_list = adata.var[['highly_variable', \n",
    "                      'dispersions_norm']].sort_values('dispersions_norm', \n",
    "                                                        ascending=False)[0:n_hvgs].index.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Startegy 2: Targeted Genes.\n",
    "gene_features = []\n",
    "for entry in list(adata.obs['guide_id'].unique()):\n",
    "    for element in entry.split(';'):\n",
    "        if element != 'nan':\n",
    "            gene_features.append(element.split('_')[0])\n",
    "gene_features = list(set(gene_features))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Combine the 2 gene lists into the full feature set\n",
    "gene_features = adata.var_names[adata.var_names.isin(gene_features)].tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "gene_features = list(set(gene_features+hvg_list))\n",
    "gene_features = [gene for gene in gene_features if gene not in perturbed_conditions_list] # This prevents leakage\n",
    "print('gene_features: ', len(gene_features))\n",
    "# print(gene_features)"
   ]
