    "## 2. Model training\n",
    "\n",
    "**Model setup**: As discussed in Task 1, we set up a `Pipeline` combining the `StandardScaler` and the implemented model.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: I tested several models with varying degrees of success under different set ups. For the final submission, I think the `Ridge` had the best training times for hyperparameter tuning, ability to work with the multioutput task of predicting multiple values per observation and still showed relatively high performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "731c917d-d494-410a-8b80-01053b2d7196",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`KFold`: K-Fold cross-validator. \r\n",
    "Provides train/test indices to split data in train/test sets. Split dataset into k consecutive folds (without shuffling by default \r\n",
    "\r\n",
    "Each fold is then used once as a validation while the k - 1 remaining folds form the training set."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "a71668a2-891c-4226-b6b0-b0fe28074945",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cv = KFold(n_splits=CV_splits, shuffle=True, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8d0f0b04-3e86-4c74-a7d1-ac51d0401394",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.1 Ridge regressor"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "adb30a0c-18b5-43ea-80a3-1ffa5d2c1405",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ridge_pipeline = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "    (\"model\", Ridge(random_state=RANDOM_STATE))]\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1d3e6cdb-2ba5-4d6f-a354-cf5a8aa96b7b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 2.1.1 Hyperparameter tuning"
   ]
  },
